.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt ASSERT 3
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm assert
.Nm __assert_fail
.Nd assertion failure
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In assert.h
.In assert.h
.Fn assert "int expression"
.Ft void
.Fn __assert_fail "const char *expression" "const char *file" "unsigned int line" "const char *function"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn assert checks an expression. When the expression is false it reports the failure and
aborts the process. .Fn __assert_fail is the internal reporting entry used by the macro.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn assert does not return on failure. .Fn __assert_fail does not return.
.Sh ERRORS
No errno value is set; the failure terminates the process.
.Sh STANDARDS
ISO C23; ring 0.
.Sh CAVEATS
The diagnostic text follows the glibc form, not the historical BSD form. See H-13 and C41.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr abort 3
.Xr libc 7
